 Thunderbolt Fighters landed after a daylight sortie over France , they were painted in the usual drab green camouflage colour and both had a pink and red glamour girl on the side about twenty feet long , typical of the Yanks", "context_len": 50}}}, "fashioned": {"freq": 12, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 25, "context": "And I went up and down the road and miles away then came back and I could n't stop because this bike was very old fashioned and you had to stop it by pedalling back", "context_len": 35}, "UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 4, "context": "er , the old fashioned working horses er practically extinct", "context_len": 10}}}, "roots": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 15, "context": "yes , erm my wife came from the Midlands , from Coventry and her family roots were in Coventry at the Midlands , in fact there she still has numerous nieces and nephews and great nephews and great nieces there to this day , my with the exception of a sister who moved , who , to Basildon , erm I have two brothers and er they still live in London , still live in East Ham , er the distance is not too great erm and , but obviously as we get older the amount of visiting we do will be constricted by the difficulties of getting from Harlow to East Ham especially when one is compelled to stop driving a motor car", "context_len": 124}}}, "uprooted": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "about three years ago he uprooted and went to Guildford", "context_len": 10}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "uprooted all these old trees and things", "context_len": 7}}}, "writers": {"freq": 10, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 38, "context": "People keep writing letters to the Mercury saying how can we afford to spend time and money debating this , well they can afford the time and the money employing out of work newsreaders to produce videos and writers and photographers to produce their glossy magazines , their glossy leaflets I did n't need the R S P C A or the League to tell me that er , the fox photo , this fox photo was a fake , I mean that 's obvious to anybody I did n't need them to tell me that the video was suspect , that too is obvious", "context_len": 105}}}, "theatres": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "the theatres and", "context_len": 3}}}, "wales": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 0, "context": "Wales , that 'd be too far would n't it , to travel", "context_len": 13}}}, "travel": {"freq": 29, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 13, "word_index": 82, "context": "I would have thought if she would have sat in the chair , I mean well she could n't go the week aha I do n't young enough yeah , about a month ago she just peed of somewhere and some , I do n't know , she 's alright , I said yes she 'll be alright , I said I 'm going to start cooking so she said I got to take these Heather , I said well they 'll travel better in there , your father said you know Jane he said if you 'd given her a hand", "context_len": 102}, "NOUN": {"freq": 16, "word_index": 35, "context": "The belief of the City Council is that , notwithstanding there are clearly difficult traffic problems in the city , there is more opportunity to encourage people to use other more environmentally friendly modes of travel by locating development in and on the edge of the main urban area , a view that 's supported by P P G thirteen and the research document onto planning , transport and planning emis planning and transport emissions on which it was based", "context_len": 80}}}, "vicinity": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 20, "context": "er , well , Guil erm he wanted to er , go to Guildford I presume because that 's his vicinity for doing all his work you see ?", "context_len": 29}}}, "commute": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "Should be able to commute and", "context_len": 6}}}, "c