nd you used to have to handle all that with forks , muck forks , they used to call them , and that was big biggest fork and by God , they used to pull your heart out", "context_len": 49}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Erm or any other little fork lift there which the quarry belonged then", "context_len": 13}}}, "trampled": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "You can guess what it was like , straw and everything , being trampled down all winter , sodden with with water and everything", "context_len": 24}}}, "sodden": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "You can guess what it was like , straw and everything , being trampled down all winter , sodden with with water and everything", "context_len": 24}}}, "heaps": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 44, "context": "Sugar beeting in those days , you used to stick the old plough in , plough them up and then we had to go along knocking them , to knock all the soil off , then chop the tops off , put them in heaps , go along with the old horse and cart", "context_len": 54}}}, "furrow": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 12, "context": "the o the old farmer used to go along with his one furrow plough , and a pair of good horses , and it was no mean feat", "context_len": 28}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "plough": {"freq": 12, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 13, "context": "the o the old farmer used to go along with his one furrow plough , and a pair of good horses , and it was no mean feat", "context_len": 28}, "UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 16, "context": "Erm I told him he ought to get erm , one of these rotovators and a plough underneath", "context_len": 18}, "VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 1, "context": "to plough your way through", "context_len": 5}}}, "feat": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 27, "context": "the o the old farmer used to go along with his one furrow plough , and a pair of good horses , and it was no mean feat", "context_len": 28}}}, "tractors": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 62, "context": "It , it , it just went on for a lit a short time afterwards but er , but when the war ended course things , some things changed pretty rapidly as you can appreciate but , but by this time I , I was working for Ellwells then on long distance transport and we used to have to go and fetch tractors or bulldozers that had got armour plating on from Dagenham docks and bring them up here and start selling them to civic contractors and the , the Americans were selling a lot of equipment as well at end of the war , and I saw money made overnight like , people were buying the lorries and putting them on the road you know for work", "context_len": 128}}}, "ploughed": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 58, "context": "I mean today , you 've got to be an educated man to know how to even , they 've got er tractors and everything , but in those days you 'd got to set your plough furrow out so as you you could run your plough down your first one , and then as you as you ploughed your first furrow out you 'd got to plough your next one into it", "context_len": 73}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 31, "context": "I agree , sometimes I can tell you I have witnessed a hunt and on a cold , frosty morning when er about forty or fifty horses are thundering across the ploughed field , it 's enough to p the power of that sight is enough to make the hairs on the back of your neck stand up that 's not what we are against the hunter that came to me and says Eh up lad , I wo n't go drag hunting because I 'm sixty years old , I 've done it all my life and I like the ride , I like to be there I never see a fox killed that 's fact , it 's in the video", "context_len": 123}}}, "stubble": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "One in the furrow and one on the stubble , see ?", "context_len": 12}}}, "blade": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "And you used to do that at a ten inch blade all day , up and down that field", "context_len": 19}, "NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 11, "context": "We used to ma , we used to buy the scythe blade and", "context_len": 13}}}, "mowing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "Day in and day out , today they can Same with old mowing machines , they used to go out To open a field up in those days , they used to have to go round with a scythe", "context_len": 39}}}, "scythe": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 7, "context": "It it was all cut with a scythe until er well I started I go to Holland to work when I was fourteen and my brother Charlie he got away and my father and mother was left they were home", "context_len": 40}}}, "swathe": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "Go right round a f these the field and cut your first swathe out and tie it up with a a load of the straw that you 'd cut and bind it up , bundle it up and shove that in the hedge bottom", "context_len": 44}}}, "bind": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 30, "context": "Go right round a f these the field and cut your first swathe out and tie it up with a a load of the straw that you 'd cut and bind it up , bundle it up and shove that in the hedge bottom", "context_len": 44}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "Or you can select it and then say bind er and then deselect it and then pick it up and move it", "context_len": 22}}}, "bundle": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 34, "context": "Go right round a f these the field and cut your first swathe out and tie it up with a a load of the straw that you 'd cut and bind it up , bundle it up and shove that in the hedge bottom", "context_len": 44}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "A fall is what we call you know a bundle of", "context_len": 11}}}, "hedge": {"freq": 10, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 42, "context": "Go right round a f these the field and cut your first swathe out and tie it up with a a load of the straw that you 'd cut and bind it up , bundle it up and shove that in the hedge bottom", "context_len": 44}}}, "binder": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 4, "context": "Then the old old binder used to come in with two two year old stalwarts , horses , and he used to go round this field and it used to take him days", "context_len": 33}}}, "stalwarts": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "Then the old old binder used to come in with two two year old stalwarts , horses , and he used to go round this field and it used to take him days", "context_len": 33}}}, "shears": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "You used to get two shears underneath your arm like that , and they used to drop them down like that , across your knees and top them like that , see ?", "context_len": 33}}}, "stook": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "And you used to put eight to a stook , that was so it would dry out , you see ?", "context_len": 21}}}, "leading": {"freq": 29, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 23, "word_index": 64, "context": "game erm , I like the one about you go to the last supper and the waiter spills soup on your trousers , the waiter , ha tell you else about the Marx brothers an'all , the waiter is er the king of Snowdonia and it 's Groucho Marx , the , they 've got this massive hall , and er these big steps leading down into it you know and as , as they 're coming in there 's somebody at the top and Ann says who 's , who 's walking in and they walk down the stairs you know and Mr and Mrs and the king has you know and he says oh the king Snowdonia is about to arrive , he should be here", "context_