 some of the guys as well , one of the things that lorry drivers and policemen do have very much in common is that we have pr probably one the shortest erm pension lives of most professions", "context_len": 69}}}, "chased": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 6, "context": "I have seen away supporters being chased up the road into Pleck Park and but erm I think basically a lot of the trouble used to be caused by drink and now they do n't have any drink in the ground they er they , they seem to have cracked that one", "context_len": 52}}}, "truncheon": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 86, "context": "And er they drew their truncheons , that I 'd never seen before , policemen with truncheons , er and they started to run and everybody else started to run , and I forgot there was a puppy dog , this puppy dog it it chased it chased towards the er p policemen , and started er barking and d and carrying on , and one of the policemen did no more than thump it straight across the top of the head with a with a truncheon , and er and that was the end of the puppy", "context_len": 98}}}, "scamper": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "Well everybody everybody really er began to scamper", "context_len": 8}}}, "dived": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 22, "context": "Er , people would try front doors to see if they could get in front doors , but no , and they dived down er er er entrances between the between the houses and so on", "context_len": 36}}}, "entrances": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 27, "context": "Er , people would try front doors to see if they could get in front doors , but no , and they dived down er er er entrances between the between the houses and so on", "context_len": 36}}}, "baton": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 33, "context": "Er , and all in all , it was quite er it 's quite it was quite an experience , er 