ndex": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "bombing": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 99, "context": "The other time I remember was when William the chromium platers in Street ye got bombed , with a high explosive bomb , but there was , there was no one hurt that I remember , and then the Halleys the tent people had an incendiary bombs and got burnt out , at the same night that they dropped some incendiary bombs on the bus depot in Road , they , they were a lot of work for the fire brigade , but comparatively speaking with , with Birmingham I think Walsall got off very lightly as regards the bombing , as there was no heavy industry around here", "context_len": 109}, "VERB_PresC": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 50, "context": "Erm well the solution to that was to hold the meetings of the General Assembly , where the hostile American majority was , but not to permit a vote to be taken on any resolution and this meant that President Johnson could pursue his , his then secret plan of bombing the north without any hostile United Nations resolution being passed against it", "context_len": 63}}}, "comma": {"freq": 17, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 14, "word_index": 38, "context": "er the air force , the German air force , aye , they had a go as well , they they they they they they they were providing all sorts of er er strafing and bombing , er comma", "context_len": 39}, "VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 2, "context": "Yeah sausages comma erm we can have what we like ca n't we", "context_len": 13}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Eggs so comma but all of them just before the last one", "context_len": 12}}}, "contention": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "overly": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "Er and this particular time of the year , it was summer of course , you we you you were n't overly worried about not having a shelter , you see", "context_len": 31}}}, "quartermaster": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "Er er it seems we had a very good er er quartermaster , he seemed to always turn up er he seemed to always turn up with something", "context_len": 28}}}, "longest": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 13, "context": "Although , although I would think that er Waldo Gregory has got the longest er time served in active service than probably er any other individual that went to Spain", "context_len": 30}}}, "wounds": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 9, "context": "Survival instinct is absolutely incredible , to see the wounds of a terrier and a fox when they have locked jaw locked and are pulled squealing out of a hole , I think I am deeply concerned about anybody here today that can turn that blind eye because what their terrier men are doing is dog fighting , make no bones about it , they wo n't be interested in laying the scent , they will not be interested in being retrained and helping your fraternity", "context_len": 86}}}, "stones": {"freq": 9, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 9, "word_index": 64, "context": "twenty would own a motor car and we 're now faced with the probably one in three have a motor car , we 're now faced with a problem which can only detract from life in the town , also the fact that huge lorries are passing through what were envisaged as quiet residential neighbourhoods with a consequent breaking of curbs and of paving stones where the lorries are compelled to mount the pavings in order to get round parked cars and things of that nature it detracts from the life in Harlow I do , I think a considerable extent , erm , the other factor is that there 's become a lack of pride in the town by the people who live in it , this", "context_len": 128}}}, "butts": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "They they were n't against laying about you with sticks and stones and rifle b