 American system and if er the president manages to get something through congress , you can bet that very quickly the president will face some defeat in congress shortly thereafter to remind the president that the United States does not have , contrary to the popular press , does not have a presidential system of government", "context_len": 109}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 36, "context": "There are areas , one or two of which I will go on to elude to , which I still think are actually going to make for the greatest savings in the coming financial year and thereafter", "context_len": 37}}}, "flows": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 37, "context": "Make it a team if you like you know get all the all the other bits of stuff that you know all the other knowledge get that coming in all working together so the whole thing just flows up and down nicely instead of", "context_len": 44}, "NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 26, "context": "Surely where the boundaries are around rural settlements , whether or not there are boundaries around rural settlements , does n't flow from E two but flows from decisions that district councils are free to make at the moment", "context_len": 39}}}, "charges": {"freq": 13, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 11, "word_index": 38, "context": "It , it 's really because as somebody gets older the risk gets very , very great , and it needs all the money that 's built up in the early years to sustain the risk , the charges for the risk later on , in the later years", "context_len": 49}, "VERB_PresT": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 8, "context": "Mind you my regular 's back and she charges three pounds", "context_len": 11}}}, "subscriptions": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "Last autumn it was stated in a document that there would have to be further subscriptions of finance before er , the project became profitable", "context_len": 25}}}, "assessing": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"f