cize union officials , yet secretly at the end of each week , their pay packet shows no deductions for trade union fees", "context_len": 37}}}, "freeloading": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 34, "context": "Congress , this motion would make the rulebook obligation for all shop stewards to honour that duty and to freeload members not just from the exploitation of employers , but also the exploitation of freeloading", "context_len": 35}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "principles": {"freq": 14, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 14, "word_index": 57, "context": "Er , I make the point I think that , erm , we should oppose the er , Deregulation Bill if it 's based on providing deregulation by Ministers , because I think that 's a constitutional point that is of great import , but the , the rest of it erm , are really sets of principles that I hope you 'd agree to , subject to amen amendment and dis discussion , because the information that we got is that the consultation period is going to be very tight indeed , and that it might not be able to go through the normal committee procedures in order to put things through erm , with er , proposals in that , er , in that respect", "context_len": 127}}}, "stewards": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 12, "context": "Congress , this motion would make the rulebook obligation for all shop stewards to honour that duty and to freeload members not just from the exploitation of employers , but also the exploitation of freeloading", "context_len": 35}}}, "freeload": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "Congress , this motion would make the rulebook obligation for all shop stewards to honour that duty and to freeload members not just from the exploitation of employers , but also the exploitation of freeloading", "context_len": 35}}}, "consolidation": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "That membership consolidation is important , but with check-off and other payment methods and the issue of computer printed cards valid for two years , we feel that there are alternatives and better methods to investigate", "context_len": 36}}}, "pill": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 13, "context": "See , they 've got most women hooked on , on er contraceptive pill for all their reproductive life and they 're dead keen that we should all get so worried about menopause that we would also be buying their products until we die !", "context_len": 45}}}, "clump": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "If you look from towards , which was a large house in a clump of trees , at the far side was a pavilion which was the clubhouse , they used to hold air displays and pleasure flights , also they had commercial flights", "context_len": 44}}}, "pavilion": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 32, "context": "Well some of them came by road and RAF trucks , the fuselages , and then there were all they started at the top of the airfield in the old flying club pavilion , and then they were er stripped down and stuff was taken off them , checked out , for airworthiness to see whether it was ready to go back on the planes , and then they came down to the back of the top hanger which was then they were all down to the skeleton of the aircraft and they started rebuilding them again like , there were engine shops and the place at the bottom hanger where they used to make the Swallow side-cars was the spraying and where they completed the aircraft", "context_len": 127}}}, "clubhouse": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 27, "context": "If you look from towards , which was a large house in a clump of trees , at the far side was a pavilion which was the clubhouse , they used to hold air displays and pleasure flights , also they had commercial flights", "context_len": 44}}}, "motorbikes": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 34, "context": "The club 's planes were usually Tiger Moths in the main , and as I remember the main airport building adjacent to the main road , pre war , were building Swallow side-cars for motorbikes", "context_len": 35}}}, "crashing": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Well I remember an Oxford aircraft over-flying the airfield and crashing in blocking the lane and going into the hedge on the other side , into Gingers Yard", "context_len": 28}, "VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 50, "context": "No , not precisely I , I was a bit too young then , I , I remember all the songs about her Amy wonderful Amy and all those and oh and when she married Jim I was very much in but I could n't actually say I remembered her crashing at Walsall The erm you could , yeah , when I came home from work one Monday afternoon my nan said this eighty eight had gone over very low , and we , we heard that they 'd dropped this landmine this same aircraft had dropped this landmine that had gone under the gas holder at the gas works , in Road and the , they had some rescue workers from the A R P to get", "context_len": 128}}}, "blocking": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 58, "context": "And Thomas and John Smith , who I 've just mentioned were actually a split family , Thomas Smith was erm so loyal that when the first round of parliament , sorry , when the first Royalist troops came into Oxford , he , as a J P prosecuted some of the citizens who tried to stop them blocking down Botley Bridge as a defence measure", "context_len": 66}}}, "comics": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 23, "context": "Billingham Woolwork we used to get entertainment nearly every lunchtime in the canteen , sometimes it was a film or live acts , comics and singers and one of the workers named Haydon , formed a small band which he call Butch Blood and the Boston Bashers", "context_len": 47}}}, "dispersal": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 38, "context": "No they used to have organized ENSA concerts and er such like and er , when the Americans started arriving in England in large numbers ready for D Day , the temporary placement depot at Lichfield was a dispersal unit for soldiers sent there", "context_len": 44}}}, "memorable": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "They sent their big band for a show and it was a really memorable sound as they had fellas on the way over to join Glen in Europe", "context_len": 28}}}, "sergeant": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 3, "context": "An American army sergeant arrived at the airport one day who befriended me and he was in charge of an artillery spotting plane called the Piper Cub which they gave a small corner of the airfield to", "context_len": 37}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Er The sergeant downstairs , if he sees any trouble or he finds something that 's going off or bumps into something , then he can radio back into base again", "context_len": 31}}}, "befriended": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "An American army sergeant arrived at the airport one day who befriended me and he was in charge of an artillery spotting plane called the Piper Cub which they gave a small corner of the airfield to", "context_len": 37}}}, "spotting": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 21, "context": "An American army sergeant arrived at the airport one day who befriended me and he was in charge of an artillery spotting plane called the Piper Cub which they gave a small corner of the airfield to", "context_len": 37}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Train spotting in East Anglia will take on a whole new meaning", "context_len": 12}}}, "stripes": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 11, "context": "He came in one afternoon and started painting black and white stripes round the fuselage and wings , when asked the reason for this he said it was a new allied marking", "context_len": 32}}}, "fuselage": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 66, "context": "to b build wings for the planes that finally came up to the airport down there and erm it was very much a structural set-up as I say I used to have to take plates down there from the airport to be normalized , it was er a sort of softening treatment for aluminium and made them easier to shape and rivet them onto the main fuselage , but they , they used to make Harvard wings and cowls , engine cowls , for the Bostons and Havocs they were n't the one type of Boston was a fighter bomber and another one it had the front navigator 's position cut out and they used to have a search light put in there which they used to call", "context_len": 128}}}, "allied": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 30, "context": "He came in one afternoon and started painting black and white stripes round the fuselage and wings , when asked the reason for this he said it was a new allied marking", "context_len": 32}}}, "marking": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 19, "context": "And then when we come in , the assessment form is written out and erm er there 's a marking sheet which I 'll I 'll sh sh show you before we go out on the road", "context_len": 37}, "VERB_PresC": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 19, "context": "Art checked his books , there were a lot of little marks on the end papers , other readers marking their patch no doubt , defiling narrative as dinosaurs have devoured other less fortunate in the past no doubt", "context_len": 39}}}, "landed": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 11, "context": "Later in the year , two U S A Thunderbolt Fighters landed after a daylight sortie over France , they were painted in the usual drab green camouflage colour and both had a pink and red glamour girl on the side about twenty feet long , typical of the Yanks", "context_len": 50}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "erm Undoubtedly the university erm with it 's connections with the aristocracy and the landed gentry and the church was mainly royalist , but that is not to say that it all was", "context_len": 33}}}, "sortie": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "Later in the year , two U S A Thunderbolt Fighters landed after a daylight sortie over France , they were painted in the usual drab green camouflage colour and both had a pink and red glamour girl on the side about twenty feet long , typical of the Yanks", "context_len": 50}}}, "drab": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 25, "context": "Later in the year , two U S A Thunderbolt Fighters landed after a daylight sortie over France , they were painted in the usual drab green camouflage colour and both had a pink and red glamour girl on the side about twenty feet long , typical of the Yanks", "context_len": 50}, "UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "camouflage": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 27, "context": "Later in the year , two U S A Thunderbolt Fighters landed after a daylight sortie over France , they were painted in the usual drab green camouflage colour and both had a pink and red glamour girl on the side about twenty feet long , typical of the Yanks", "context_len": 50}}}, "glamour": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 36, "context": "Later in the year , two U S A Thunderbolt Fighters landed after a daylight sortie over France , they were painted in the usual drab green camouflage colour and both had a pink and red glamour girl on the side about twenty feet long , typical of the Yanks", "context_len": 50}}}, "fortress": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": null, "context": null,