nful , reporting character", "context_len": 50}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "weakening": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "The move should help stimulate economies on the continent where recession has been weakening the market for British exports", "context_len": 19}}}, "exports": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 18, "context": "The move should help stimulate economies on the continent where recession has been weakening the market for British exports", "context_len": 19}}}, "boosted": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "The news boosted shared prices to a new record", "context_len": 9}}}, "believing": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 6, "context": "The city welcomed the move , believing the rate cut 'll be followed throughout Europe , particularly on the continent where German decisions still dominate economic policy making", "context_len": 28}}}, "downward": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 27, "context": "But with inflation there on its way down and the economy bumping along the bottom of a recession , the Bundesbank Council decided it could tolerate another downward step", "context_len": 29}}}, "dominate": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 26, "context": "Okay , but saw does n't C command Florence because the first branching node dominated saw , it 's a verb phrase and that does n't dominate Florence , it 's on the wrong branch", "context_len": 35}}}, "knowingly": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "While Britain was in the E R M until September last year , our interest rates could never knowingly undercut those of Germany", "context_len": 23}}}, "undercut": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "While Britain was in the E R M until September last year , our interest rates could never