ll be the relations between the federal government and South Carolina , any attempt to do this would be on his part a naked act of usurpation", "context_len": 42}}}, "federal": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 16, "context": "Er as you can imagine in the circumstances of the civil war the government , the federal government , was much vexed about the question of spies and fifth columnists and people er in the , in the northern states er engaged in sabotage and collecting espionage of , of various kinds so er Lincoln suspended the writ of habeas corpus", "context_len": 61}}}, "usurpation": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 41, "context": "Apart from the execution of the laws the executive has no authority to decide what shall be the relations between the federal government and South Carolina , any attempt to do this would be on his part a naked act of usurpation", "context_len": 42}}}, "endure": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 22, "context": "if you remember the question that the founding fathers faced was how do you create a government which is strong enough to endure and to defend the nation and defend the country yet a government which is not so strong that it erodes the rights of individuals within it , this is the , the essence of the , the problem of government as , as the founding fathers saw it", "context_len": 71}}}, "erodes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 42, "context": "if you remember the question that the founding fathers faced was how do you create a government which is strong enough to endure and to defend the nation and defend the country yet a government which is not so strong that it erodes the rights of individuals within it , this is the , the essence of the , the problem of government as , as the founding fathers saw it", "context_len": 71}}}, "suspended": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 55, "context": "Er as you can imagine in t