y would lead to a centrally appointed Police committee at least fifty percent and a centrally appointed chairman , paid by the Home Secretary much rather like the Leicestershire Health Authority and of course this will severely undermine the local democratic accountability of the Police service", "context_len": 80}}}, "steelworks": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "The mines , the steelworks , the shipyards , all killed off and with them communities killed off", "context_len": 18}}}, "shipyards": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "The mines , the steelworks , the shipyards , all killed off and with them communities killed off", "context_len": 18}}}, "gains": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 57, "context": "The humble people bring up the hero as their own child , eventually the hero realizes through a dream , through a prophecy , a visitation or something that he is not the child of his humble parents , but the find out who his real parents were , and then returns and arduous struggles and eventually gains his rightful place", "context_len": 61}}}, "crafts": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "The same way as the steel workers , the coal miners and the skilled crafts people", "context_len": 16}}}, "obscene": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 6, "context": "Now , they would be thought obscene public perception has changed and understood that animals are sentient beings and that we demean our humanity if we are cruel to them or permit cruelty", "context_len": 33}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "The fact is that any so called sport which involves the exhaustion , distress and eventual death of an animal has got to be obscene in the eyes of any human being", "context_len": 32}}}, "macho": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 30, "context": "As more and more decisions are being taken by management at local level , we need to ensure our local representatives have the necessary skills to cope with the new macho management techniques", "context_len": 33}}}, "techniques": {"freq": 9, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 9, "word_index": 49, "context": "And then a bit of a roundabout route coming back , trying to get a variety of road , and any areas of the drive which we can look at , we will , discuss amongst ourselves , practise one or two things , maybe one or two little techniques", "context_len": 50}}}, "freezes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "They 've seen the introduction of performance related pay , personal contracts , new working practices , pay freezes , pay cuts and always the fear of redundancy and all of this has been going on at a time when increasingly companies are withdrawing from national collective agreements , are establishing separate bargaining arrangements , restricting the activities of trade union officials and increasingly de-recognizing trade unions", "context_len": 67}}}, "withdrawing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 43, "context": "They 've seen the introduction of performance related pay , personal contracts , new working practices , pay freezes , pay cuts and always the fear of redundancy and all of this has been going on at a time when increasingly companies are withdrawing from national collective agreements , are establishing separate bargaining arrangements , restricting the activities of trade union officials and increasingly de-recognizing trade unions", "context_len": 67}}}, "bargaining": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 52, "context": "They 've seen the introduction of performance related pay , personal contracts , new working practices , pay freezes , pay cuts and always the fear of redundancy and all of this has been going on at a time when increasingly companies are withdrawing from national collective agreements , are establishing separate bargaining arrangements , restricting the activities of trade union officials and increasingly de-recognizing trade unions", "context_len": 67}}}, "restricting": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 55, "context": "They 've seen the introduction of performance related pay , personal contracts , new working practices , pay freezes , pay cuts and always the fear of redundancy and all of this has been going on at a time when increasingly companies are withdrawing from national collective agreements , are establishing separate bargaining arrangements , restricting the activities of trade union officials and increasingly de-recognizing trade unions", "context_len": 67}}}, "longstanding": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 13, "context": "That means making what might have to be some very difficult decisions affecting longstanding practices and even loyalties that have developed over many years", "context_len": 24}}}, "harsher": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 13, "context": "Could it be that er evolution in sort of Aboriginal societies are more harsher than that allowed for a more experienced man to teach a young child how to live as opposed to , it , it 's beneficial for", "context_len": 40}}}, "regrettably": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "We 've seen new and harsher disciplinary procedures introduced , safety measures ignored and regrettably increases in the number of cases of racial and sexual harassment", "context_len": 26}}}, "harassment": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 25, "context": "We 've seen new and harsher disciplinary procedures introduced , safety measures ignored and regrettably increases in the number of cases of racial and sexual harassment", "context_len": 26}}}, "merger": {"freq": 31, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 31, "word_index": 23, "context": "I mean in so I I come here today with a petition that I presented that also talks about proposing to abolish the merger , I mean this is a move just one step away from that but I still feel in what was proposed at the last full council meeting and I would express my views to the officers that in light of what has been suggested today is actually implemented to the wording as it stands because the joint working party that had been er written up previously never did meet although if I can inform it was only the officers who actually met up and I hope that in light of all the working group and the two heads of centres covering for each other", "context_len": 128}}}, "vibrant": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 25, "context": "Let 's be honest , I did n't wan na see good sections , I wan na see strong sections , I wan na see vibrant sections , but I also want to see the truth in those documents when it comes back afterwards , so I 'm disappointed on this issue and er I hope something in future will be done about to report the real things that we discussed at conference as well", "context_len": 75}}}, "refusal": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 86, "context": "Erm , on page thirty you talk about the erm Employer 's Federation in the er minimum terms and conditions , well I 'm only hoping that my own firm Securicor do n't have any er input into that , because er as you know they unilaterally reduced all the terms and conditions Securicor guarding and cleaning recently erm I 'd like to know when we intend meeting with Securicor Cleaner I do know you 've written to them on a number of occasions and their refusal to meet with us", "context_len": 91}}}, "timers": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 41, "context": "I know that we 're meeting with the company next week , but whether or not anything 's come forward on that and also erm in reference to the pensions section , erm , just correct your deliberate mistake and part timers ca n't enter the Securicor Pension Scheme", "context_len": 49}}}, "grievances": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 113, "context": "know that a lot of you must work at places where you 've got guards on the gate and we all should take a bit of interest in going to see these guards , find out that they 're working for two pound or two pound forty an hour , they 're working as many hours a week as they 'll actually work with no overtime rate , no night rate , no benefits worth having and I mean really I wish you 'd go to your companies and try and arrange site allowances , cos that 's the only way we 'll get any improvements , but when we talk about resolving grievances , we just took in Yorkshire region someone to a tribunal for constructive dismissal", "context_len": 128}}}, "cowboys": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 4, "context": "Securicor have joined the cowboys on the contract guarding and really I mean you must be getting sick of us getting up every time about security guards , but it 's an important problem and you must know that a lot of you must work at places where you 've got guards on the gate and we all should take a bit of interest in going to see these guards , find out that they 're working for two pound or two pound forty an hour , they 're working as many hours a week as they 'll actually work with no overtime rate , no night rate , no benefits worth having and I mean really I wish you 'd go to your companies and try and", "context_len": 128}, "VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "My interest in North Plains people in 1750 to 1850 which is about the same period for the you know cowboys goes back many years to my pre- writing days", "context_len": 30}}}, "dismissal": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 127, "context": "know that a lot of you must work at places where you 've got guards on the gate and we all should take a bit of interest in going to see these guards , find out that they 're working for two pound or two pound forty an hour , they 're working as many hours a week as they 'll actually work with no overtime rate , no night rate , no benefits worth having and I mean really I wish you 'd go to your companies and try and arrange site allowances , cos that 's the only way we 'll get any improvements , but when we talk about resolving grievances , we just took in Yorkshire region someone to a tribunal for constructive dismissal", "context_len": 128}}}, "motions": {"freq": 15, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 15, "word_index": 21, "context": "Frankly I think from our colleagues in the conservative party should n't really be wasting our time here with these silly motions , erm what 's needed is if you 're gon na improve the housing situation in the city and in the country as a whole , we need to be allowed to use our capital receipts , all the ones we 've piled up , and we need to also inject money into the national economy to build new homes and incidentally to get the economy moving again and start bringing down the level of unemployment", "context_len": 98}}}, "retrying": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "We 've been retrying to get recognition nationally and locally for fifteen years", "context_len": 13}}}, "licensing": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 10, "context": "Okay , but the item that licenses them the other licensing sentence you need in order to license these items , you ca n't just go anywhere in the sentence so sentence three , herself saw Florence is no good , even though Florence is there , it 's in the wrong place relative to herself and similarly six , anyone saw no one is no good , even though no one is in the sentence", "context_len": 76}}}, "synonymous": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 9, "context": "County Council believes that this advice and guidance is synonymous with the view that is taken that development of the open countryside will in fact represent the exception rather than the rule and that new development would not normally be permitted", "context_len": 41}}}, "thanking": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Could I firstly start by thanking those delegates who after Congress yesterday have expressed support about the two rule changes that we lost and to give some encouragement to new delegates here that even if you get up here and you lose it , there 's some one hell of a lot of support out there on the floor", "context_len": 59}}}, "memberships": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 26, "context": "We 're not talking about individual members saying I wan na go here or I wan na go there , we 're talking about groups of memberships within these sorts of branches", "context_len": 32}}}, "easiness": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "Surely the needs of the members should come before the administrative easiness of putting people into sections for the Union and as I 've said who better to judge where they need to go and what their needs are than the members themselves", "context_len": 43}}}, "utilities": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 39, "context": "The members ' case must come first , otherwise everyone is gon na be put into the odds and sods section which is Apex , because it has n't got a subject such as public services or energy and utilities", "context_len": 40}}}, "organizes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "This Union faces strong competition in almost every sector in which it organizes", "context_len": 13}}}, "loyalties": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 53, "context": "erm The warden of Merton had to get out of Oxford quick when the king arrived , because , and spent the erm war in London , name was Nathaniel Brent , and he was quite an important man in the organisation of the Parliamentary war effort , and Lincoln had rather mixed loyalties , too", "context_len": 56}}}, "ample": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 33, "context": "I do n't see that that pu that the the staff comment , which is gon na be the first thing need have anything to do with the child at all there is ample place", "context_len": 35}}}, "worded": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 17, "context": "My general position would be that if this policy is to go ahead the more it 's worded in the positive rather than the negative the better", "context_len": 27}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "The P P G seven has a very clear theme about supporting rural diversification , it is positively worded P P G", "context_len": 22}}}, "railways": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 3, "context": "Looking at the railways I would n't go anywhere near the station though I might oh hang on I mean what does that all mean ?", "context_len": 26}}}, "underfunding": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 29, "context": "At the moment we have old and dirty trains which are expensive to use , with many rural towns without a railway at all through years and years of underfunding", "context_len": 30}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "It is obvious the way the railway should move forward not privatization but a reversal of the underfunding and a move to a total commitment of higher financial support", "context_len": 29}}}, "privatizing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Privatizing what is the first thing the government do to make B R more attractive to the private sector ?", "context_len": 20}}}, "announces": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Announces a huge redundancy programme that will lead erm which will result in a lot more unstaffed stations and a hell of a lot less maintenance", "context_len": 26}}}, "poorest": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "Our rail network is the lowest funded , the lowest staffed and has the lowest investment programme in Europe with the poorest quality service and the fastest declining level of safety , but B R has the highest fares", "context_len": 39}}}, "privatized": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Now I ask you , do you think that a privatized network that has to pay a divided to investors will lead to a better , safer , cleaner , cheaper railway ?", "context_len": 33}}}, "unprofitable": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 14, "context": "For us the customers , it will mean higher fares and fewer services as unprofitable and social services are cut and this is only if we are left a train service at all", "context_len": 33}}}, "operators": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 36, "context": "Colleagues , great credibility should go to John Prescott , Shadow Transport Secretary , who has demanded that all foreign registered tankers should provide details of routes when they set off from port so that all operators can be dealt with", "context_len": 41}}}, "immoral": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 19, "context": "I mean I do n't , I do n't believe that your government is stupid er it may be immoral on occasions , it may be wrong but I do n't believe it 's necessarily stupid", "context_len": 36}}}, "fights": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 27, "context": "Congress , the vote in the House of Commons was lost unfortunately , but our sponsored MPs must ensure that the opposition in the House of Lords fights this ridiculous legislation as vigorously as possible , and we must support our brothers and sisters in B R with their fight", "context_len": 50}}}, "vigorously": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 32, "context": "Congress , the vote in the House of Commons was lost unfortunately , but our sponsored MPs must ensure that the opposition in the House of Lords fights this ridiculous legislation as vigorously as possible , and we must support our brothers and sisters in B R with their fight", "context_len": 50}}}, "seconding": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 4, "context": "But I think in seconding this motion I think it 's a way forward and I think it 's better late than never I think what it talks about that we would not be here today Mr Chairman if this would have been agreed by what was put by the officers two and half years ago", "context_len": 56}}}, "dogma": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 52, "context": "My supplementary is will the Chairman of policy and resources committee make a statement to the county council to reassure and inform the ethnic minority community and the general public of Leicestershire of the need for tolerance and racial harmony and reaffirm the county council 's opposition to all forms of racist dogma", "context_len": 53}}}, "unattractive": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "I come from Norfolk and with privatization many rural lines will be cut as the private sector being as unattractive and unprofitable", "context_len": 22}}}, "holidaymakers": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "Services which provide trains for both rural villages and holidaymakers will be cut", "context_len": 13}}}, "fattened": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "Cuts have already begun to as the British Rail cow has fattened up", "context_len": 13}}}, "subsidy": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 44, "context": "The Department of Transport , they were very little help , we contacted them and after initial propaganda visits , we were told that sixty thousand tons of traffic was n't worth bothering about it was n't large enough to warrant any help or subsidy", "context_len": 45}}}, "spillage": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "w