rd countryside , wider countryside , the countryside and open countryside , indicating perhaps some of the difficulties in in erm identifying exactly what area it is that would be covered by a Policy E two", "context_len": 76}}}, "refusing": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 58, "context": "Now question is whether or not there is a simple ability to realise a capital receipt and use it I think , and if that were true , if what you 're saying is true and there was some net gain to be made very easily then I think we would have a hard time , perhaps , refusing what you 're saying", "context_len": 63}}}, "modifications": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "perverse": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "to me that it would be perverse of us to fall into the trap if we were to do so of endorsing Policy E two and not know that what we were endorsing was in fact what the Secretary of State specifically rejected on the grounds perhaps that it was unduly restricted or detailed or inappropriate for some of those other reasons that are set out in the earlier part of that notice of approval", "context_len": 75}}}, "endorsing": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "presumption": {"freq": 10, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 37, "context": "I read in the Planning Press that the Newbury District Council managed to browbeat the the Department of Environment into accepting the phrase in their in a local plan , so perhaps presumptions are er the word presumption may or may not be acceptable , but then to extend it into saying well you ca n't even say , not normally be acceptable , and , not normally be er agreeable , for any sort of policy er means that strategic policies or general policy approaches are simply ruled out ri right across the board", "context_len": 95}}}, "planting": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "Yes erm Policy E two was at that time was er relating to programme of tree planting er", "context_len": 18}}}, "resume": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Can we resume at twenty past eleven please ?", "context_len": 9}}}, "divergence": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 33, "context": "No , from that figure of forty nine point nine five percent above S S A in nineteen ninety one we proposed a budge that had brought reductions year on year in that divergence of view", "context_len": 36}}}, "determinate": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "This in my view is a critical determinate of leaving aside the question of fifty of fif the application of section fifty four A that determines whether the policy is required", "context_len": 31}}}, "comers": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 45, "context": "And I 'm sure the districts a lot has been said about er it being the districts ' view that well you know we 've got this policy so we will we will exercise a high level of restraining to protect the countryside against all comers etcetera etcetera", "context_len": 48}}}, "inquiries": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 36, "context": "Erm and I I ca n't help wondering , this is perhaps something that Mr Donson may well want to come back to , erm what Mr Donson 's position would be at subsequent local plan inquiries where local plans were to contain such policies and there was was n't to be a strategic basis er for those policies", "context_len": 59}}}, "presumptions": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 32, "context": "I read in the Planning Press that the Newbury District Council managed to browbeat the the Department of Environment into accepting the phrase in their in a local plan , so perhaps presumptions are er the word presumption may or may not be acceptable , but then to extend it into saying well you ca n't even say , not normally be acceptable , and , not normally be er agreeable , for any sort of policy er means that strategic policies or general policy approaches are simply ruled out ri right across the board", "context_len": 95}}}, "phrasing": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "Policy E two as proposed is a very common form of phrasing used by planning authorities to circumvent the Government objection to presumption against policies", "context_len": 25}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "tea break and I like that , I like the er the phrasing", "context_len": 13}}}, "presuming": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 23, "context": "So I said if it 's only for a mile it 's going to be well less than a minute at eighty , presuming you were doing more than thereabouts and er that was it", "context_len": 35}}}, "deliberation": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "Strictly controlled should mean consented after the most careful deliberation and under the most carefully contrived er conditions", "context_len": 18}}}, "contrived": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "Strictly controlled should mean consented after the most careful deliberation and under the most carefully contrived er conditions", "context_len": 18}}}, "obverse": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "I do n't think they 've seen it 's obverse side", "context_len": 11}}}, "sucker": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "You would be drawing sucker from E two in your anti-development policies in your local plan", "context_len": 16}}}, "recollection": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Erm I I 'm speaking from recollection sir at having looked into this in the context of planning appeal which is now a little while ago , but it did strike me at the time that er there was a definite feeling that the agricultural issue was very strong protection of ag agricultural land throughout was a strong issue up to er the mid nineteen eighties and certainly was up to the time in late seventy nine early nineteen eighty and er therefore there was a feeling that Policy E three simply er was supplementary to those other policies", "context_len": 99}}}, "connotations": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 36, "context": "Erm the second point I 'd like to make is er we danced round this phrase presumption this morning , I 've tried to avoid using it because its its it gets all sorts of er connotations going", "context_len": 38}}}, "browbeat": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "I read in the Planning Press that the Newbury District Council managed to browbeat the the Department of Environment into accepting the phrase in their in a local plan , so perhaps presumptions are er the word presumption may or may not be acceptable , but then to extend it into saying well you ca n't even say , not normally be acceptable , and , not normally be er agreeable , for any sort of policy er means that strategic policies or general policy approaches are simply ruled out ri right across the board", "context_len": 95}}}, "minimize": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 33, "context": "But nothing has has really changed it 's surely implicit that green field sites will have to be released to meet the justifiable needs for development erm that there are ways clearly to minimize the impact by by first redeveloping the existing sites by by releasing sites in less sensitive locations , or developing sites that have minimal impact on on existing settle settlements or patterns of development un unless in exceptional circumstances there is for example the need for a new settlement", "context_len": 83}}}, "redeveloping": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 39, "context": "But nothing has has really changed it 's surely implicit that green field sites will have to be released to meet the justifiable needs for development erm that there are ways clearly to minimize the impact by by first redeveloping the existing sites by by releasing sites in less sensitive locations , or developing sites that have minimal impact on on existing settle settlements or patterns of development un unless in exceptional circumstances there is for example the need for a new settlement", "context_len": 83}}}, "impracticable": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "I mean in some respects that 's almost an imposs an impossible task it 's simple impracticable", "context_len": 17}}}, "evolving": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "As soon as you publish a list for the exceptional circumstances it it will be overtaken by er evolving new forms of development for example", "context_len": 25}}}, "locate": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 11, "context": "Thirdly that there is no requirement to demonstrate a need to locate development in open countryside erm and we 've been reminded this morning that erm one of the erm flaws in the policy put forward back in nineteen seventy nine or eighty erm appears to be that it erm required , certainly in the explanatory memorandum , that the development be erm essential erm to er essentially have a countryside location", "context_len": 72}}}, "originating": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "Er my answer to Miss Whittaker 's originating question , there has been no argument at all that the area where this policy will operate , which is the open countryside outside of the A O N Bs and national parks , has got any special character that requires a more restrictive approach than national policy", "context_len": 56}}}, "rein": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "As I said earlier I do not think that this is an area where the district councils should be given a completely free rein to interpret the matter within their own local plans", "context_len": 33}}}, "predominantly": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "There has to be a strategic theme particularly in counties such as North Yorkshire which is predominantly rural , it is a major area of planning control , fully merits strategic control and that strategic control must be applied or if it if it is to be applied in the structure plan if you do agree that there should be a Policy E two , then the control of development must be applied consistently over the districts", "context_len": 77}}}, "agriculturalist": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Er being an agriculturalist rather than a planner I tend to get a bit confused by higher planning semantics of the difference between strict control and presumption against not normally", "context_len": 30}}}, "feeble": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 14, "context": "Er and I think I came up with six negatives and and one very feeble positive", "context_len": 16}}}, "discourage": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Paragraph three , discourage most forms of development", "context_len": 8}}}, "counteract": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Now to counteract that the only positive one I could find was , while accepting that some development in the open countryside may prove to be necessary", "context_len": 27}}}, "pronouncements": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 26, "context": "Now it seemed to me that was n't a very erm reasonable balance and er comparing that with the with the Secretary of State 's recent pronouncements where he talks about local planning authorities needing to breathe fresh life into the countryside through their development plans and I want local planning authorities in rural areas to give the need to diversify the rural economy as much priority priority in their thinking as protecting the countryside and the two go hand in hand , and comparing those two er points I I would I would put to North Yorkshire the question , Do they think that the explanatory memorandum is is consistent with that er policy statement from the Secretary of State ?", "context_len": 122}}}, "flaws": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 30, "context": "Thirdly that there is no requirement to demonstrate a need to locate development in open countryside erm and we 've been reminded this morning that erm one of the erm flaws in the policy put forward back in nineteen seventy nine or eighty erm appears to be that it erm required , certainly in the explanatory memorandum , that the development be erm essential erm to er essentially have a countryside location", "context_len": 72}}}, "focuses": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Erm the fourth advantage I would say is that it focuses on the balance between the need to promote rural enterprise and the need to protect the countryside", "context_len": 28}}}, "habitats": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 44, "context": "Just picking up on Professor Lock 's point earlier on about changes in the nineteen eighties or since the nineteen eighties , erm as in my statement I have suggested that there has been a substantial loss of nature conservation interest and wild life habitats both in this county and throughout the country", "context_len": 53}}}, "demonstrable": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 41, "context": "And indeed I would remind the panel that we still have in P P G one that the basis of appli applications for development should be allowed having regard to development plan and all material considerations unless proposed development would cause demonstrable harm to interests of acknowledged importance", "context_len": 48}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 33, "context": "And it seems to me that in order that that ought to be reflected in any revised wording of the of the policy that the development should be permitted unless it would could demonstrable harm", "context_len": 35}}}, "generality": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 55, "context": "Erm I 'd like to refer to my page three or er section four in my conclusions because I think if I if I heard Professor Lock correctly I think he and I are at one in in a suggestion which is is put to you in in if you like without prejudice to the generality of what I have been saying in support of the council 's policy", "context_len": 69}}}, "papered": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 23, "context": "But I mean the the panel is going to have to explore this apparent conflict which I do n't think 's been properly papered over between what is in paragraph five of P P G one and section fifty four A", "context_len": 41}}}, "tourist": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "Erm I think that would apply to er some of the existing tourist policies erm certainly and some of the recreation policies", "context_len": 22}}}, "unsympathetic": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 39, "context": "As far as Mr Collier 's point er alternative policies concerned , I think listening to it and only half having perhaps digested the full implication , I think really as a matter of principle we 're not un unsympathetic to a lot of what what a lot of people are suggesting there", "context_len": 53}}}, "fudges": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "However , I think we do still have some certainly some reservations about erm the policy and how it perhaps fudges some of the loca locational provisions of existing policies", "context_len": 30}}}, "locational": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 25, "context": "However , I think we do still have some certainly some reservations about erm the policy and how it perhaps fudges some of the loca locational provisions of existing policies", "context_len": 30}}}, "polity": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "Just one point on perhaps on what Mr Donson was saying about the need for polity statement", "context_len": 17}}}, "mitigate": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "It does n't er really sort of er er in a sense prevent er or mitigate against a lot of a lot of developments in the countryside", "context_len": 27}}}, "disputes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "Does this policy not in effect strengthen the county 's arms in , arm in such disputes ?", "context_len": 18}}}, "directs": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 54, "context": "Er yes I raised an example without referring to a specific site and the site is in Richmondshire where the county council has objected to a proposal in erm what is a a local plan in its very formative stages and the proposal conflicts with Policy I five in so far as I five directs development to the main towns and urban areas", "context_len": 63}}}, "batter": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "Does n't it give you two policies rather than one to batter Mr Earle with , or his colleague ?", "context_len": 20}}}, "countervailing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "We 're quite content that we 're going to have to er put before the local plan system the the countervailing issues and the weight that 's given to the countryside through E two is appropriate in the circumstances", "context_len": 39}}}, "ambiguities": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "A lot of the dis discussion has clearly been erm trying to resolve some of the ambiguities in P P G seven er and I think perhaps different perception to what sort of countryside in North Yorkshire we are trying to safeguard through through policies", "context_len": 45}}}, "accumulative": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "And the consequences of a latter approach could lead to accumulative change in the appearance and nature and character of the countryside so that you get something rather different than most people 's perception of a countryside being there for its own sake", "context_len": 43}}}, "dilute": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "abiding": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "Erm I 'm not sure whether there 's an abiding need to to actually bring it all back together again in in the context of a summary", "context_len": 27}}}, "dissect": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 27, "context": "I do n't think er my only comment would be that having heard all the comments that have been made and listened to them and tried to dissect them and understand them , I do n't think they really alter er fundamentally our position", "context_len": 44}}}, "julian": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 0, "context": "Julian shut up , just cos you know just cos you", "context_len": 11}}}, "perspectives": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Erm just three perspectives from a district level on on matters that have been raised", "context_len": 15}}}, "warranted": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "First of all erm Ryedale District is n't saying that the policy is warranted because North Yorkshire is in any unusual regardless of the quality of the countryside here , but that this is a reasonable reflection of national policy on development in the open countryside", "context_len": 46}}}, "precludes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "And thirdly , with regard to Mr Donson 's concern erm I do n't feel that the policy precludes the provision of low cost housing on exception sites , er certainly hope it does n't", "context_len": 35}}}, "showman": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 41, "context": "I 've got a lovely bunch of coconuts , they 're all standing in a row , big ones , small ones , one 's as a big as head , oh give a twist , of the wrist , the showman said", "context_len": 43}}}, "gypsy": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "He wanted to be a gypsy , what they used to called them , then", "context_len": 15}}}, "bate": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 26, "context": "Well to tell you the truth , I went to own school , when it was er winter , when it comes the winter , they bate somewhere for the winter , do you see ?", "context_len": 36}}}, "hoopla": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "What had er boats , we had hoopla , and er a coconut shy , , what you call it", "context_len": 20}}}, "coconut": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 12, "context": "What had er boats , we had hoopla , and er a coconut shy , , what you call it", "context_len": 20}}}, "cornfields": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "And on this side , erm corn , cornfields", "context_len": 9}}}, "cottons": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 32, "context": "I remember going to 's school , and er they put in front of us , I were very young , put in front of us a lot of s colours , cottons", "context_len": 33}}}, "pavements": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "Hopscotch , when we 'd got a pavement , we 'd more fields than er pavements", "context_len": 16}}}, "saddle": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "And er horses Oh I could saddle a horse and r I can ride a horse , no not racing horses , you know , but I can just ride them", "context_len": 31}}}, "cherries": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "And er I remembering Dad , once he bought a cherry tree , and went up to get all these here cherries off the trees , and when we got them we used to wipe them and put them in a bag , and sell them at the fairs", "context_len": 49}}}, "skittles": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "lodging": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 26, "context": "Well me first job was d er down lace market , and I worked in Street , Hill , and at the back there was all lodging houses , do you see ?", "context_len": 33}}}, "dinnertime": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 16, "context": "And what they used to sell a er er at er in the lace market at dinnertime , they used to make a big roly pudding , like that , with jam in it and sauce on it , white sauce , it was more water than sauce , you know ?", "context_len": 52}}}, "kippers": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 29, "context": "And under the bed there was a basket , and we used to see the chap come down and wash these , what was in the mass it was kippers , and conga eel", "context_len": 34}}}, "conga": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 32, "context": "And under the bed there was a basket , and we used to see the chap come down and wash these , what was in the mass it was kippers , and conga eel", "context_len": 34}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "Then they used to come down the street , I 've got some lovely conga eels , stinks a bit , but not a deal", "context_len": 25}}}, "eel": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 33, "context": "And under the bed there was a basket , and we used to see the chap come down and wash these , what was